CORE
temporal_assumption1.sv
--aig --bound 5
^\[main\.assume\.1\] always \(main\.a \|=> main\.b\): UNSUPPORTED: assumption not supported by netlist BMC engine$
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.r -> main\.b: INCONCLUSIVE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The netlist BMC engine cannot add an assumption with a temporal
operator to the netlist.  Such an assumption must not be silently
dropped, as this is unsound: the property holds under the assumption,
but would be reported as REFUTED without it.  The assumption is
therefore marked UNSUPPORTED, and the dependent property INCONCLUSIVE.
